  "theorem_name": "Q3PrimePrefixProductParityObstruction",
  "declared_proposition": "For every l>=0 let T_l=6*3^(6l+2)+3 and let P_l be the product modulo 3 of the first T_l primes after omitting the prime 3. If the mod-3 prime race ties at T_l, then P_l=1 modulo 3. Consequently P_l=-1 modulo 3 is a sufficient exact certificate excluding the TICKET-260 compatible prefix. Moreover asymptotic density balance alone cannot exclude these ties.",
  "mathematical_argument": "A tie has N_1=N_2=(T_l-1)/2=3*3^(6l+2)+1, an even integer. The product of all nonzero residue symbols is (-1)^N_2=1 modulo 3. Its contrapositive proves the product-minus-one certificate. For the density-only no-go, prepend the unique zero symbol and then alternate +1,-1 forever. Every ordinary prefix discrepancy is at most one, the two symbol densities tend to one half, yet every T_l-1 is even and there is an exact tie at every special prefix. The three actual finite certificates have product -1, but no all-l product theorem is proved.",
  "result_classification": "partial_theorem",
  "problem_status": "open_not_proven",
